@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Demonstrates layered packaging with <<import>> and <<access>>
'                 stereotypes and inward-pointing dependencies
'   usecase:      Educational example showing dependency-inversion in a clean
'                 layered architecture
'   complexity:   medium
'   domain:       E-commerce
' ============================================================================
title Example Package Diagram - Multi-module Layered Architecture

' ============================================================================
' LAYERED ARCHITECTURE (Clean / Hexagonal style)
' Packages are arranged in horizontal LAYERS. The Dependency Rule states:
'   dependencies must point INWARD toward the domain/core.
'   - Outer layers may depend on inner layers.
'   - Inner layers must NOT depend on outer layers.
' UML stereotype keywords on dependency arrows:
'   <<import>>  - public contents of the target are merged into source's namespace
'   <<access>>  - source references names from the target without merging
'   <<merge>>   - full private merge (rare; not used here)
' ============================================================================

' ---- INFRASTRUCTURE LAYER (outermost) - technical details & frameworks ----
package "Infrastructure" <<layer>> {
  package "Persistence" {
    class OrderRepositoryImpl
    class ProductRepositoryImpl
  }
  package "Messaging" {
    class EventBus
  }
  package "Web" {
    class RestControllers
  }
}

' ---- APPLICATION LAYER - orchestration, use cases, app services ----
package "Application" <<layer>> {
  package "OrderServices" {
    class PlaceOrderUseCase
    class CancelOrderUseCase
  }
  package "CatalogServices" {
    class SearchProductsUseCase
  }
  package "Ports" {
    interface OrderRepository
    interface ProductRepository
  }
}

' ---- DOMAIN LAYER (innermost) - pure business rules, no framework deps ----
package "Domain" <<layer>> {
  package "Orders" {
    class Order
    class OrderLine
  }
  package "Catalog" {
    class Product
    class Price
  }
}

' ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
' DEPENDENCY DIRECTIONS - every arrow points INWARD (toward Domain).
' Outer packages <<import>> the ports they implement; inner packages
' stay ignorant of the outer ones (dependency inversion via interfaces).
' ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

' Web (outer) depends on Application use cases to handle requests
Web .down.> OrderServices : <<access>>
Web .down.> CatalogServices : <<access>>

' Application use cases depend on Domain entities
OrderServices .down.> Orders : <<import>>
CatalogServices .down.> Catalog : <<import>>

' Application defines Ports (interfaces); use cases depend on the ports
OrderServices .down.> Ports : <<import>>
CatalogServices .down.> Ports : <<import>>

' Infrastructure implements the Ports (dependency inversion)
' The implementation arrow points inward to the port interfaces.
Persistence .up.> Ports : <<implements>>

' Messaging is used by Application to publish domain events (inward rule)
Messaging .up.> OrderServices : <<access>>

note right of Domain
  <b>Dependency Rule:</b>
  Nothing in Domain depends outward.
  Arrows only ever point <i>into</i> this layer.
end note

@enduml
